messages:
Priya (SE): Quick heads-up — ZenithBank POC kicks off tomorrow AM. They asked for: streaming NDJSON events, in-stream function/tool calls that return structured records, resume-on-drop behavior, and short presale pricing for a 2-week trial. Any immediate red flags?
Tom (Sales Eng): Token estimate ~70k tokens/day, bursts to 200k. They want predictable tail-latency. Can we do short-term reserved capacity or a burst buffer?
Eve (Solutions): No red flags. Recommend: small reserved box + burst pool, disable large batch aggregation for this POC to keep latencies low. I'll add SLO hints for them.
Jose (Security): Requirements from their side: SOC2, IP allowlist, ephemeral STS creds for tooling, and a basic DPA addendum. Hosted POC OK with invite accounts; Private/VPC requires infra lead.
Priya (SE): Request: need runnable Node and Rust snippets showing: 1) SSE or WS streaming with NDJSON per event, 2) function/tool declaration and handling of tool_result (final validated JSON), 3) resume handshake with last-seq ack.
Eve (Solutions): I'll assemble a one-pager and example repo. For NDJSON, recommend treating the final tool_result as canonical; incremental chunks may not be valid JSON.
Tom (Sales Eng): Pricing ask: can Finance quote a 2-week small reserved with 3x burst tokens and a flat POC support fee? I'll capture numbers once we have suggestions.
Eve (Solutions): For latency, set model config: batching: "off", kv_prefix_cache: "on", max_concurrency_per_conn: 8. That keeps single-request latencies stable.
Priya (SE): Node example (SSE):
```js
// minimal streaming + tool handling
const stream = client.stream({model: 'redwood-small', streaming: true, response_format: {type: 'ndjson'}})
stream.on('data', evt => {
  if (evt.type === 'tool_call') {
    // payload is a JSON string per NDJSON record
    const rec = JSON.parse(evt.payload)
    handleRecord(rec)
  }
  if (evt.type === 'tool_result') {
    // final validated JSON array/string
    finalize(JSON.parse(evt.payload))
  }
})
stream.send({prompt: '...'}).catch(console.error)
```
Priya (SE): Resume note: include header 'x-rwd-session' and send last-ack seq in query ?last_seq=NN. Server will replay cached KV up to that seq and continue. If client cannot resume, fall back to a fresh session (may redo tokens).
Tom (Sales Eng): Do we provide schema enforcement? Customer wants strict object shape for records.
Eve (Solutions): Yes. Use response_schema in the request. Example (concept): response_schema: {type: 'array', items: {type: 'object', properties: {id: {type:'string'}, amount: {type:'number'}}}}. Runtime will validate and emit tool_result or tool_result.error.
Jose (Security): Also: audit logs for requester and per-request token usage must be exportable for them. We can enable extended retention for the POC if needed.
build-bot: Example repo created: github.com/redwood/examples/zenith-ndjson-poc (canary-20240316)
Tom (Sales Eng): Great. I'll ask Finance to price 2-week reserved-small + 3x burst. Also asking Legal for quick DPA + subprocessor list.
Priya (SE): Small gotcha to call out to Zenith infra: if they post-process tool_result, recommend they run our SDK helper validate_schema(payload) to catch drift.
Eve (Solutions): I'll drop the one-pager link and attach the minimal Node/Rust snippets, plus a checklist: invite accounts, IP allowlist CIDRs, STS role, and acceptance of NDJSON output.
Tom (Sales Eng): Thanks team. I'll update the customer and loop back when Finance/Legal confirm. :+1:
